+          "read": "2026-11-04",
+          "said": "4.1 … (b) each and every producer, director, script supervisor and scriptwriter must be a permanent resident of Hong Kong aged eighteen (18) years or above; … 4.2 The proposed mini-series (“Mini-series”) shall have at least six (6) episodes, with the running time of each episode of at least forty-five (45) minutes. It shall be a fictional narrative (animated series and docuseries not included). … 6.3.3 … ten (10) Applications as Phase 2 projects … will receive a cash prize of a minimum of $600,000 for a six (6)-episode Mini-series, with $100,000 for each episode from the 7th episode up to $1,200,000 being the maximum amount … 6.4.2 … not more than four (4) Mini-series (“Phase 3 Projects”) will be selected. … will receive a cash prize of $4.5 million for producing the Pilot Episodes. … the cash prize shall only be used for production of the Pilot Episodes and shall not cover any other expenses such as promotion and marketing, distribution etc. … 6.5.5 … it can of its own volition seek funding from other investors, financiers and/or streaming platform operators to finance the production of the remaining episodes of the Mini-series. Unless with the approval of the Government, the completed entire series can only be released on streaming platforms which are on the list of streaming platforms to be specified by the Government from time to time and are available to viewers in Hong Kong within the first three (3) years upon the completion of the Pilot Episodes. If the Selected Phase 2 Company secures funding to finance the completion of the entire Mini-series, the entire series shall only be available on streaming platforms on a subscription basis in the first year of release."
